WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.384
Host: Trace C5–T1 through the plexus and
explain how the cords are named.

2
00:00:05.384 --> 00:00:10.702
Guide: Ventral rami C5–T1 form upper, middle
and lower trunks,

3
00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:19.840
Guide: each dividing into anterior and
posterior divisions. These combine into
lateral, medial and posterior cords,

4
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:26.243
Guide: named relative to the second part of
the axillary artery, and then give terminal
branches.

5
00:00:26.243 --> 00:00:32.342
Host: A diagram labels the posterior cord.
Posterior relative to what?

6
00:00:32.342 --> 00:00:35.561
Guide: The second part of the axillary artery.

7
00:00:35.561 --> 00:00:41.154
Guide: The artery provides the conventional
landmark for brachial-plexus cord names.
